customer_message:
@AppleSupport So like I said from the start you can’t turn it off fully from the control centre. 
“If you want to completely disable Wi-Fi and Bluetooth for all networks and devices, follow these steps:
To turn off Wi-Fi, go to Settings &gt; Wi-Fi and turn off Wi-Fi.”

conversation_context:
@AppleSupport 3 updates now and still have not fixed the problem of swiping up and being able to turn off or on WiFi and Bluetooth, why. Samsung is becoming more attractive everyday.
@139274 In iOS 11 and later, when you toggle the Wi-Fi or Bluetooth buttons in Control Center, your device will immediately disconnect from Wi-Fi and Bluetooth accessories. Both Wi-Fi and Bluetooth will continue to be available. More info here: https://t.co/G7BHuQnDS6
@AppleSupport When you turn it off from the settings it says “off” and does not connect randomly. If you turn it off from the control centre it says “not connected” in the settings and connects sometimes randomly.
@139274 This is expected behavior with the iOS 11 updates. The Control Center function is a quick disconnect feature that will only disconnect your current connection. To disable, you'll want to go into your settings. For more information, please visit: https://t.co/G7BHuQnDS6

